    "paragraph": "The first study generated dense Middle Layer Super Output Area origin-destination matrices for England and Wales by fusing travel survey and mobile network data to segment weekday morning peak trips by seven modes and eight purposes. Another paper co-designed and developed the Urban Model Platform in collaboration with the City of Hamburg to serve as a public backbone for modeling and simulation in urban digital twins. Finally, researchers developed and evaluated seven spatial models to automatically delineate village territory boundaries across 1,059 villages in North and Centre Benin.",
